# Shell scripts must keep LF endings in the working copy, whatever the machine.
#
# With core.autocrlf=true (the default on Windows), a checkout rewrites text
# files to CRLF -- and a CRLF shell script fails at its shebang with
# "/bin/sh^M: bad interpreter". That applies to deploy/antigravity-proxy/
# entrypoint.sh, which is the container's ENTRYPOINT: a Windows-side checkout
# would build an image that cannot start.
#
# Docker builds from a Linux clone are unaffected, which is what makes this the
# kind of problem that only appears for whoever tries it locally first.
*.sh text eol=lf
